From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:50:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] tests: switches that take a mechanism away, one option at
 a time

The snapshot cycles and the oracle read option switches from the
environment on the commits that have the option (a compile-time switch
per option, since a field a commit lacks is a build that fails): the
published scan snapshot, the published block forms, the writer's upkeep
level, the thread's alert poll, the tables carried across a merge's
rewrite and the scan snapshot carried across a publish. The cut
schedule takes the rewrite's carry away too.

Where a seal cannot be held, the cycles' seal lands before they begin:
a commit that joins a finished seal publishes the forms into the state a
snapshot holds, and whether the seal had finished by the first commit
was the machine's load, which made the oldest commits fail or pass by the
hour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011ZkLidS5BYuaBXVcvPAkdd
